CEO Secretary,AIFIAN,Mobile Apps,Management / Business,Secretary,Full-time,Entry level,"Neihu District, Taipei City, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,"['Secretary', 'Administration']","About AIFIAN
AIFIAN is at the forefront of transforming real-world asset investment globally. Our mission is to democratize access to smart investment opportunities, leveraging advanced technology to bridge traditional finance and modern accessibility. Following our successful soft launch in Taiwan in 2023, focusing on the burgeoning market of liquor investments, we've captured significant enthusiasm. As we prepare to scale our operations internationally, we're expanding our team to champion AIFIAN's vision worldwide.
About the Role
Weâ€™re looking for someone who thrives in a support role and takes pride in being the key player that ensures everything runs smoothly. This position is perfect for someone who enjoys taking ownership of important tasks behind the scenesâ€”whether itâ€™s managing the CEOâ€™s schedule, coordinating projects, or solving unexpected challenges. You will be a vital part of the team, proactively ensuring that all operations are efficient and organized. If you take pride in being a reliable and adaptable team member who thrives on getting things done and supporting the wider goals of the organization, this could be the perfect fit for you.
What You'll Do

Handle a range of administrative office tasks, such as organizing documents, ordering office supplies, and processing expense reimbursements.
Provide operational support for various business projects to aid the CEO teamâ€™s objectives.
Collect, organize, and analyze business data to produce insightful reports that assist the CEO in decision-making.
Organize all aspects of domestic and international travel for the CEO, including booking flights, accommodations, and detailed itineraries.
Coordinate and manage the CEOâ€™s daily schedule, including both internal and external meetings.
Tackle urgent tasks and adapt to new priorities, providing quick solutions as needs arise.
Collaborate with the People team to plan and organize internal events, ensuring every detail is covered for smooth execution.
Manage communications and documentation with external partners, like car dealers and insurance companies, including overseeing contracts and relevant paperwork.
Maintain strong relationships with our car leasing customers by offering support and handling any unforeseen situations that may arise.","What We Look For

Over two years of experience in administrative or secretarial roles, experience supporting senior management is strongly preferred.
Precision in daily tasks, ensuring all details are accurately managed.
A positive attitude toward challenges, with strong stress resilience and a willingness to embrace new tasks.
Strong time management skills with the ability to prioritize tasks effectively under pressure.
Fluent in both English and Mandarin Chinese, with strong communication skills in diverse cultural environments.
Adaptability and a proactive approach to problem-solving in dynamic environments, offering constructive suggestions.
Detail-oriented and comfortable working with numbers, proficient in Google Sheets, Google Docs, and similar office software.
Hands-on problem-solving mindset, committed to following through and ensuring smooth task completion.
