[Corporate] IT Procurement Specialist,KKCompany,Internet,Management / Business,Purchasing,Full-time,Entry level,"Nangang District, Taipei City, Taiwan",1,3 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"KKCompany Technologies Group is a leading technology group in software services. We have created the worldâ€™s first legal music streaming platform, KKBOX, and are an international software technology group focused on â€œmultimedia technologies, digital cloud, and AI applicationsâ€� as our core business to create value for the customers. The group consists of self-owned brands including KKBOX, BlendVision, and Going Cloud with enterprise customers across Asia. KKCompany Technologies has attained OpenChain ISO/IEC 5230 and ISO 27001 third-party international certification.
We have over 500 employees across offices in Tokyo, Singapore, Taipei, Kaohsiung, and Hong Kong. For more information please visit our website: www.kkcompany.com and blog: blog.kkcompany.com
The IT Procurement Specialist is responsible for supporting IT purchasing activities, managing vendor coordination, and ensuring efficient procurement operations. This role plays a key part in securing cost-effective and timely acquisition of IT products and services, while ensuring compliance with company policies and vendor agreements. The specialist collaborates with IT, Finance, and Legal teams to streamline procurement workflows and optimize IT asset management.
Responsibilities:

Process purchase requisitions, ensuring alignment with procurement policies and approval workflows.Review IT procurement requests, validating specifications, pricing, and compliance requirements.Liaise with IT vendors and suppliers, ensuring timely order fulfillment and service delivery.Assist in contract documentation and negotiation, ensuring favorable terms and risk mitigation.Obtain competitive quotes from vendors, comparing pricing, service levels, and contract terms.Track software licensing, cloud service subscriptions, and hardware purchases to optimize IT spending.Conduct cost analysis and reporting, supporting budgeting and financial planning.Maintain accurate records of IT assets, software licenses, and renewals.Ensure procurement activities align with IT asset lifecycle management strategies.Monitor contract renewal dates, subscription plans, and warranty coverage.","Requirements:
Bachelorâ€™s degree in Business, Supply Chain, Information Technology, or a related field.3-5 years of experience in IT procurement, supply chain, or purchasing.Familiarity with IT purchasing processes, vendor negotiations, and contract administration.Proficiency in procurement software, ERP systems, and Microsoft Office Suite.Strong organizational, analytical, and negotiation skills.Ability to track procurement requests, manage vendor relationships, and analyze costs.
Nice to Have:
