"Associate Account Executive, APAC (Competent English ability required)",Cake,SaaS / Cloud Services,Management / Business,Event Management,Full-time,Entry level,"Taipei City, Taiwan",2,No requirement for relevant working experience,"40,000 ~ 70,000 TWD / month","['Account Executive', 'Client Management', 'Marketing Campaigns']","About Cake
Established in 2016 in Taiwan, Cake is an international talent community and platform providing comprehensive solutions for job seekers. By offering AI tools for resumes and portfolios, job search strategies, networking resources, and international job opportunities, Cake meets all needs in career development. With over 7 million users worldwide and collaborations with over 10,000 companies, Cake helps talent find the most suitable place at different stages of their careers.Â 
Cake Business Team Culture
Values that are the foundation of our team culture, which every member embodies:
Raise the Bar - Impact matters. Stay focused and curious.Think Big & Hustle - Push for bold, thoughtful, and rapid innovation.People First - Prioritize development and wellbeing. Help people flourish and feel valued.Transparency Builds Trust - Communicate with candor, honesty, and respect.Strength through Inclusion - Welcome all voices. What makes you unique makes us all strong.One Team, One Dream - Pride and passion for our mission. Work collaboratively and have fun.
Â 
Job Intro
At Cake, we partner with top-tier companies across a wide range of industries to organize premier talent matching events. Having successfully hosted high-impact events such as the Google International Talents Hiring Event,Â Cake 2024 Career FairÂ and the 2024Â Digital & International Talent Job Fair, we are poised for even greater expansion. As we continue to increase the number and diversity of these events, we are seeking dedicated Account Executives to join us and drive our future success.
As an Account Executive at Cake, you will play a pivotal role in our recruitment events, with a focus on campaign planning and execution. This role requires a dynamic individual capable of both detailed project management and high-level strategic thinking. If you fit this description, join us to contribute to our growth and be a key player in connecting top talent with leading companies.
Â 
Responsibilities
You'll be working closely with our cross-regions Business Teams and Marketing Teams to achieve our global mission - building the largest talent pool in APAC.
Event Leadership:Â Lead and execute recruitment events in collaboration with companies, initiating impactful business activities to boost brand awareness and revenue. This includes overseeing all campaign marketing details, tracking performance / budget, and managing event execution (online, offline, and hybrid).Customer Obsession:Â Act as the primary contact and trusted advisor for customers, offering guidance and setting clear expectations for program execution.Integrated Communications: Develop and oversee strategies for integrated communications, including PR, digital, and social marketing.Strategic Partnerships:Â Drive strategy for pitching potential partners and maintain a robust network of strategic partnerships.Performance Tracking and Quality Management: Efficiently oversee day-to-day account activities, track account budgets and service levels, and provide input on staffing hours. Review all reporting efforts, monitor results against annual goals, and drive customer satisfaction.","Minimum Qualifications
Effective communicator with fluentÂ English skillsEager to develop a career in a position that can actually create impacts to the worldQuick learner who is resourceful and driven to tackle hard problems in a dynamic, fast-paced environmentSelf-Starter who is determined to lead change and make a real impactCritical thinker who is passionate about creating and implementing solutionsProject management skills â€” capable of setting goals, tracking progress, and collaborating effectively with cross-team stakeholdersEffective coordinator who is able to lead teams from marketing, business, and tech from backgrounds to get things doneResults-oriented and always focusing on driving results in a measurable way to ensure we stay focused on the highest impact initiativesHave passions in turning ideas into reality, and unlocking the unknowns in the world
Â 
Bonus Qualifications
Experience in event planning, public relations, or marketing communications (attaching a project portfolio will be a plus.)
