Project Implementation Coordinator è¨“ç·´å°ˆæ¡ˆåŸ·è¡Œå°ˆå“¡,è²¡åœ˜æ³•äººç„¡åœ‹ç•Œé†«ç”ŸåŸºé‡‘æœƒ MÃ©decins Sans FrontiÃ¨res (Taiwan),NGO,Management / Business,Project Manager,Contract,Entry level,"Zhongshan District, Taipei City, Taiwan 104",1,2 years of experience required,"45,000 ~ 60,000 TWD / month","['Microsoft Office', 'Excel', 'PowerPoint']","MÃ©decins Sans FrontiÃ¨res (MSF) is an international, independent, medical humanitarian organization that delivers emergency aid to people affected by armed conflict, epidemics, natural disasters and exclusion from healthcare. We offer assistance to people based on need and irrespective of race, religion, gender or political affiliation. We have the following vacancy and are looking for a talented individual with a strong desire to contribute to humanitarian work and commit to the aims and values of MSF to join our team in Taipei.
Project Implementation Coordinator
The Project Implementation Coordinator will work closely with the MEDICS Project Lead based in Hong Kong, the Taiwan Team, and various stakeholders in the organization and implementation of the 2025 MEDICS (Multidisciplinary Enhanced Deployment In Critical Surgical Care).  We are looking for someone who is highly organized, detail-oriented, proactive, effective communicator with good interpersonal skills and can coordinate with multiple stakeholders simultaneously. The tasks involve monitoring and implementing project plans, organizing and participating in various stakeholders' meetings, procurement, monitoring budgets and expenditures, providing administrative support, and ensuring project deadlines are met in a timely manner.

*Contract Duration: 2 June 2025 â€“ 31 October 2025.The duration of the position may be extended for an additional 2 weeks to support the implementation of MEDICS training to non-MSF participants after the original MEDICS training.
Major Responsibilities
Work closely with the MEDICS Project Lead to ensure tasks are executed according to plan and flag and resolve identified risks/issues that may impact timelines and outcomesCoordinate and implement logistics and administrative activities for the project including, but not limited to:Coordinating with the admin team in both MSF Hong Kong and Taiwan in arranging travel, hotel, visas, and other necessary preparations for travel and accommodationEnsure that all processes are completed and that all relevant regulations are followed and documentedProcure and secure necessary materials, stationaries, meals etc. needed for the trainingEnsure procurement, contracts, payments, invoicing activities, and ensure compliance with MSF Taiwanâ€™s policies and procedures; monitoring expenses to ensure adherence to the budgetLiaise/coordinate and communicate with various stakeholders (local and international)Liaise/coordinate with vendors/suppliers for the event, including securing necessary permits for the training facility, logistics, etc.Serve as the focal point for all event requirements and manage pre, during, and post-event needs.Volunteer recruitment and management, including activities briefing, debriefing, administrative work eg. meal arrangements, certificates etc.
