P&D - Warehouse Inventory Operations Specialist - Linkou,ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Logistics / Trade,Trade administration,Full-time,Entry level,"Linkou District, New Taipei, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Warehouse Inventory Operations SpecialistDo you like to be a spider-in-the-web that ensures a smooth logistics execution in the warehouses? Do you like to play a crucial role in ensuring availability of parts for our end customers? Do you want to extend your experience by working in a dynamic and fast-paced environment? Then we look forward to welcoming you in the Warehousing team within the Delivery organization of ASML!Job mission and contextIn order to stay competitive and continue to be able to deliver to our customers, ASML Supply Chain Management continuously needs to further professionalize its operation. One of the large challenges for the coming years is the standardization of the processes which we run in our (over 50) Warehouses worldwide. To facilitate the standardization we are implementing an interface with our logistic service providers to connect our ERP system (SAP) with the warehouse management system (WMS) from the logistic service providers. This set up requires this role in our organization to ensure the inventory levels between ASML and the logistic service providers are in sync.You will join the Control Tower team of our diverse warehousing department on this mission, you have the drive, cross departmental communication skills and persistence to help us to make this a success.Within this role you work for all our warehouses around the world in all time zones. We aim to organize this role with the â€˜follow the sun principleâ€™. This means we have someone available in each time zone.We are now looking for someone to strengthen our organization in Taiwan to support in the Taiwan region and the Asian time zone. The warehousing team is based at ASMLâ€™s headquarters in Veldhoven, the Netherlands. One of the inventory controllers is based in the US, one in Korea. We are building up an organization in Taiwan. Your hierarchical line is into the control tower team in Veldhoven, but you will have a base with our other delivery colleagues in Taiwan.Job description & main responsibilitiesAs an inventory controller your main responsibility is to keep the stock levels in our ERP system in sync with the stock levels in the WMS. This requires extensive knowledge of the logistics processes and the IT systems. You will work together with ASML IT teams, the worldwide teams in the local organizations and the logistic service providers to ensure the inventory management processes are executed as designed.Your responsibilities:Ensure daily stock reports are produced and any discrepancies addressed and resolved.Work closely with the IT support organization, with the local planning teams and with the 3PLManage and solve disturbances caused in the logistics processes between and within the Â warehousesMonitor the interface performance and resolve errors in the interface messages / documentsAnalyze the errors and issues and solve the root causes that prevent re-occuranceManage and control inventory stock counting / inventory accuracy checks across ASML and logistics service providersEducation Bachelor or Master in Supply Chain Management, IT, Finance or comparableExperience2 to 5 years relevant experienceKnowledge of logistics (technical) processes, especially the IT flowSAP and Warehouse Management SystemsFluent in English, Mandarin. The Japanese and Korean language is a plusRelevant IT skills in MS Office applications, ERP systems, WMS applications and interface connectionsInterest in analyzing an solving issues that occur and seek for improvementPersonal SkillsSelf-steering and structural result drivenCan do mentality and proactive attitudeStrong analytical and problem solving skillsReporting skillsWilling to travelFlexibleCultural sensitivityWorking location: Linkou, TaiwanThis position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00317775-p-d-warehouse-inventory-operations-specialist-linkou-60676e929d46e4a39d37717e700783?locale=en,1001 ~ 5000 people,æ–°ç«¹å¸‚å…¬é�“äº”è·¯ä¸‰æ®µä¸€è™Ÿå��ä¸€æ¨“,"Be part of progress.
We make machines that make chips; the hearts of the devices that keep us informed, entertained and safe. Devices that improve our quality of life and help to tackle the worldâ€™s toughest problems. We build some of the most amazing machines that you will ever see, and the software to run them. Never satisfied, we measure our performance in units that begin with pico or nano.
Whether you are a student or an experienced engineer, whether you want to design or build, work with customers or software code, we are looking for people like you to help us push technology further. Explore what we have to offer. If it sounds interesting, letâ€™s stay in touch. If it sounds right for you, letâ€™s talk about how you can be part of progress.
