CS - HMI Competence Engineer - Hsinchu,ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Engineering,Equipment Engineer,Full-time,Entry level,"Hsinchu City, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Introduction to the jobSector Customer Support is responsible for the maintenance and repair of HMI systems at customer locations. CS supports the customers in the use of these complex metrology systems in their production process. This involves transferring all relevant knowledge to support the customer in the use of these systems in their production process. CS Central enables effective support to our customers by providing technical knowledge and process support. The Competence Engineering Team supports the field offices, upgrade teams and customers through the challenging new product introduction phase of a product or upgrade package.Role and responsibilitiesâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Supporting on-site introduction of new model machines and/or new platforms to our local customer service team and customer engineersâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Manage and support new upgrades or commercial options for new and existing HMI systemsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Mature the product by driving the cycle time and performance specificationsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Transferring knowledge of new products or platforms to enable local engineers to sustain the new product by themselvesâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Keep up to date on the latest technologies by maintaining a network of specialists within the HMI communityâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Prevent issues from re-occurring by driving a structured issue resolution process and (pro) active roll-out of quality solutionsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Taking part in availability / reliability projects to help identify improvements in failure sensitivity and maintainability, and then ensuring that these improvements are implemented in new and existing productsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  FMEA/upgrade alpha test preparation and support, upgrade beta test preparation and validationEducation and experienceMaster Graduate in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Physics or Computer Science.Skillsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Ability to prioritize activities and co-ordinate a broad range of specialistsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Ability to motivate and convince others at all levels of the organizationâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Strong technical background and a drive towards solutionsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Strong analytical skillsâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Customer focusâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Stress tolerantâ€¢Â Â Â Â Â  Good communication skills (multi-cultural and towards different levelExcellent written and spoken English language skillsOther informationThis job will require that you work at customer sites across the globe for maximum 30% of the year. This includes international travel to Asia, the US and within Europe for uninterrupted periods of up to six weeks.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00321556-cs-hmi-competence-engineer-hsinchu-9b6ad0a1c4eedfc0744910edc46a03?locale=en,1001 ~ 5000 people,æ–°ç«¹å¸‚å…¬é�“äº”è·¯ä¸‰æ®µä¸€è™Ÿå��ä¸€æ¨“,"Be part of progress.
