"Entry-level / Mid-level GenAI Security Analyst, Vulcan",AIFT,Software,IT,Security Engineer,Full-time,Entry level,"Tokyo Metropolis, Japan, Hong Kong S.A.R, Dubai, United Arab Emirates, Taipei City, Taiwan, Republic of Singapore, Seoul-si, Republic of Korea",1,1 years of experience required,Negotiable,"['Risk Assessment', 'Global Teamwork', 'GenAI']","About Us AIFT is a leading firm specializing in innovative solutions to help businesses protect their digital assets. We leverage cutting-edge technologies, including artificial intelligence, to deliver comprehensive security assessments and remediation strategies. Vulcan is a groundbreaking product developed by AIFT. 
If you are passionate about making a unique impact, as well as securing the future for enterprises through delivering cybersecurity for GenAI - one of the most disruptive and fastest-growing technology trends, this is the role for you.  
Know more about how we deliver transformation at: https://vulcanlab.ai/ 
-Position Overview 
We are seeking GenAI Security Analysts with keen interest in AI security and safety and the agility to thrive in todayâ€™s fast-moving AI landscape. You will support the business in analyzing client GenAI use cases, orchestrate Vulcan assessments, and translate findings into clear executive insights. We are looking for candidates with one to three years of working experience, sharp critical thinking skills, and fluency in English; knowledge of other Asian, Arabic, or European languages is a plus. 
-
Key Responsibilities 
Collect and analyze details on clientâ€™s GenAI use cases, threat & attack surface, and solution roadmap 
Support the development of Vulcanâ€™s GenAI security solution proposals and red-team test plans, ensuring alignment with industry best practices, regional regulations, and relevant guidelines. 
Execute the assessment through the Vulcan platform in line with the project scope and objectives.  
Draft executive-level report that highlight key insights, remediation recommendations and present findings to client stakeholders.  
Research emerging GenAI risks, risk management approaches, policy developments 
Collaborate with Product and Research teams to relay client feedback and ensure Vulcan solutions and methodologies stay aligned with market needs. 
Work with Marketing team to translate engagement insights into reusable assets such as playbooks, white papers, and sales collateral. -","Qualifications Bachelorâ€™s degree with 1 to 3 years of professional experience
Skilled at simplifying complex technical ideas into clear, accessible language for varied audiences 
Engaging presentation abilities to captivate and motivate potential clients 
Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English with strong interpersonal capabilities 
Comfortable working in a fast-paced, dynamic environment with mentorship 
Critical thinker who focuses on addressing the core of a problem using first-principles reasoning -Nice to Have
Technical literacy and software engineering skills 
Exposure to technology startup or consulting  
Familiarity with NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM, ISO 42001 
