t least a Bachelor or Higher education degree in the field of:Mechatronics EngineeringIn addition you have â‰¥ 3 years of experience that is relatable to ASML. Experience with supplier collaboration is a plus.SkillsTo thrive in this job, you will need the following skills:You are a design engineer with a technical background in Mechatronics Engineering.Preferably, you have Team center and/or NX knowledgeBeing a generalist in your field of expertise, willing to dive into unknown problems and ability to operate in a multi-disciplinary team;A pioneering mindset, self-propelling, a pragmatic approach, and showing initiative;Enthusiastic and ambitious professional with ability to communicate clear and concise to peers and (potential) suppliers.Quick learner, in for a challenge, continuously drive for improvements, and enjoy achieving results together with your team.Fluency in English & Mandarin is preferred.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00324537-d-e-mechatronic-engineer-support-supplier-development-ebcc50d70d8f2850462115287a692e?locale=e