D&E â€“ Electromechanical engineer (Support Supplier development) - Linkou (Evergreen),ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Engineering,Other,Full-time,Entry level,"Linkou District, New Taipei, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Introduction to the jobWe are looking for (design) engineers who are able to translate technical needs for the DUV modules into requirements that can be transferred to local suppliers in Asia. Specifically, we are looking for experienced design engineers with electromechanical competence who can deliver Technical Product DocumentationBoth the manufacturing facility and the transfer of suppliers to Asia contribute to our vision to build a more scalable, competitive and closer-to-the customer manufacturing capability in Taiwan which is able to send qualified modules directly to our customers.You will work in a team with design- and supplier quality engineers lead by a Group lead. This team is part of the D&E Field organization with an overarching mission to increase intimacy with our customer and ASML operations (Customer Support, Repair & Re-use, Manufacturing and Strategic Sourcing and Procurement)This position is open to local hires as well as Long Term assignees within ASML.You will spend ~ six months in the Netherlands or Wilton, USA for training purposes in 2026.Roles and responsibilitiesTo translate technical needs for the DUV modules into requirements that can be transferred to local suppliers in Asia, we need design engineers with different fields of specialty who will:Clarify, update, and complete available Technical Product documentation (TPD) to accomplish TPD acceptance by supplier (TAS) ;Update TPD (in-red and/or discrepancies) via Engineering Change and qualify the new supplier part quality with production engineer;Provide technical support for all Asia supplier sourcing activities.Collaborate with development teams with in Veldhoven, Netherlands and Wilton, USAEducation and experienceYou are an engineer with at least a Bachelor or Higher education degree in the field of:Electromechanical engineeringIn addition you have â‰¥ 3 years of experience that is relatable to ASML. Experience with supplier collaboration is a plus.SkillsTo thrive in this job, you will need the following skills:You are a design engineer with a technical background in Electromechanical engineering.Preferably, you have Team center and/or NX knowledgeBeing a generalist in your field of expertise, willing to dive into unknown problems and ability to operate in a multi-disciplinary team;A pioneering mindset, self-propelling, a pragmatic approach, and showing initiative;Enthusiastic and ambitious professional with ability to communicate clear and concise to peers and (potential) suppliers.Quick learner, in for a challenge, continuously drive for improvements, and enjoy achieving results together with your team.Fluency in English & Mandarin is preferred.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00324539-d-e-electromechanical-engineer-support-supplier-developm-80a0dba10b70154