ects aimed at enhancing efficiency, innovation, management and/or product development, with focus areas such as ESG sustainability or cost reductionÂ .Follow a tailored learning journeyÂ to develop your leadership skills, strategic mindset, and interpersonal capabilities.Be guided by a senior leader, senior stakeholders from the sectors and a development coachÂ , who will empower you through your journey at ASML.Gain global experience through two 3-month international assignments (e.g., USA, and Netherlands).Collaborate with fellow trainees and colleagues at all levels of the organization and build up a broad network.Join our webinar: If you are interested to find out more about the management traineeshipÂ program and this specific recruitment process, sign up for our webinar on Monday August 18th from 19:00 to 20:00 (UTC+8) via the following link: https://recruitment.asml.com/flows/2025-asml-taiwan-management-traineeship-webinar Education and experiencePerforming well under pressure and thriving in a fast-paced environment is essential to succeed as an ASML management trainee. Here, you will need:A bachelorâ€™s, masterâ€™s or PhD degree in any technical or supply chain related backgroundÂ A maximum of 1 year of relevant working experience (internships are not included within this timeframe)You are fully graduated before January 5th, 2026Availability to start the traineeship on January 5th, 2026Preferably â€“ but not mandatory â€“ experience in extracurricular activities, such as serving as part of the board for a student association or volunteer workSkillsWorking at the cutting edge of technology, you will always have new challenges that arise and new problems to solve. Working together is the only way to achieve this. You will not work alone. Instead, you will be part of a creativeÂ , dynamic work environment where you will collaborate with supportive colleagues. There is always space for creative and unique points of view. You will have the flexibility and trust to choose how to best tackle tasks and solve challenges.To thrive in this job, you will need the following skills:Ability to understand the big picture and align efforts accordingly.Capacity to think creatively and innovatively with willingness to adapt to diverse situations.Ability to nurture relationships and interpersonal skills.Strong communication skills.A sense of resilience, learning agility, and a flexible mindset.Other informationGet ready to embark on a journey where talent meets opportunity â€“ our tailored selection process ensures the best match for your next step as a potential ASML leader. To do so, you will go through the following process:Application: Apply before Monday, September 8th, 2025 at 23:59 (UTC+8). You will receive an update on your application, at the latest, 5 working days after this deadline.Video interview: If selected, you will be invited to record your answers to a few pre-determined questions.Online interviewÂ : Should you move forward to the next stage, you will be invited to complete an online Talent Exploration Report (TER) and have a short online interview about you and the results.Selection day: If you are chosen, you will be invited to an onsite day with assessed and non-assessed sessions â€“ expected sometime middle of October 2025 (Shortlisted candidates will be notified separately.)Job offer: Shortly after the selection day, we will inform if you will receive a job offer. If so, you will be offered a full-time position, and competitive salary & benefits.For further inquiry, please send us an email at Recruitment Taiwan [emailÂ protected] Â This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00324645-asml-technology-training-program-asml-management-trainees-25abd1a80ba31d2f35f563cbbd8794?locale=en,1001 ~ 5000 people,æ–°ç«¹å¸‚å…¬é�“äº”è·¯ä¸‰æ®µä¸€è™Ÿå��ä¸€æ¨“,"Be part of progress.
