D&E Field â€“ Taiwan Factory Engineering â€“ Metrology Design Engineer,ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Engineering,Other,Full-time,Entry level,"Linkou District, New Taipei, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Introduction to the jobWe are looking for experienced metrology engineers who are able to support the assembly of the scanners of one of our DUV-systems that will be produced in this factory. The support is needed to meet the output and quality requirements for this DUV-scanner.The vision is to achieve a more scalable, competitive and closer-to-the customer manufacturing capability in Taiwan.You will work in a team of approximately 50 fte (projected to grow further) of multiple competences. You will work closely together with the manufacturing team (~70 fte), and Supplier Quality Engineers (~15 fte). This team is part of the D&E Field organization with an overarching mission to increase intimacy with our customer and ASML operations (Customer Support, Repair & Re-use, Manufacturing and Strategic Sourcing and Procurement).This position is open to local hires as well as Long Term assignees within ASML.You will spend ~ six months in the Netherlands for training purposes in 2026.Roles and responsibilitiesTo build the manufacturing capability at New Taipei Campus we need metrology engineers who will:Support the scanner setup in factory and first customer introduction with high end troubleshooting capability.Help local factory engineers to clarify if scanners issues are soft- or hardware related.Assist fast troubleshooting and unblocking of scanner shipment.Coordinate possible fast fix software changes fast fix in Taiwan and/or synchronize SW change with Veldhoven.Synchronize with software team on fix required and help testing implemented fix.On a need-to-know-basis, provide knowledge sharing sessions to local Customer Support.Communicate and synchronize with engineers & architects from other disciplines (electrical, mechatronics, physics, optics).Education and experienceYou have an inherent motivation for hands-on technical support and metrology experience supported by a bachelor or master's in physics, mathematics, or related disciplines.Andâ‰¥ 2 years of experience in a metrology design engineer role.Plus is a (relatable) hands-on experience with scanner introduction and troubleshooting metrology issues.SkillsTo thrive in this job, you will need the following skills:Being a generalist in your field of expertise, willing to dive into unknown problems and the ability to operate in a multi-disciplinary team.Is familiar with metrology troubleshooting and diagnostics tools (i.e. MANA or similar).Is familiar with process of scanner setup towards required performance of the overlay, focus, productivity.Being creative, inventive, and thinking out-of-the box to realize solutions in an ambiguous environment where not all design documentation is up-to-speed.A pioneering mindset, self-propelling, pragmatic approach, and initiative.Enthusiastic and ambitious professional with ability to communicate clearly and concisely to peers and customers combined with stakeholder management skills to operate across sites and sectors.A quick learner, in for a challenge, continuously drive for improvement, and enjoy achieving results together with your team.Reasonable fluency in English is preferred.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote per-sons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Other informationThis position may require access to controlled technology, as defined in the Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require the Company to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00323848-d-e-field-taiwan-factory-engineering-metrology-design-e-ed892ea8b7d1efef43e1acd2687809?locale=en,1001 ~ 5000 people,æ–°ç«¹å¸‚å…¬é�“äº”è·¯ä¸‰æ®µä¸€è™Ÿå��ä¸€æ¨“,"Be part of progress.
