D&E - DUV and YieldStar (YS) Electrical Design Engineer - Linkou,ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Engineering,Electronics Engineer,Full-time,Entry level,"Linkou District, New Taipei, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Introduction to the jobIn the D&E team, we have multiple D&E competences to support our factory and Asia suppliers to provide decent design solution or escalation support as local D&E team.As an Electrical Design Engineer, your mission is defining, realizing, qualifying, managing and maintaining various electronic concepts and products for existing ASML DUV and YieldStar modules.Also to support Asia supplierâ€™s development in terms of quality and cost.Role and responsibilitiesThe Electrical Design Engineer is responsible for the specification, design, realization and qualification of the electrical infrastructure and electrical (sub) modules.Desire to specify & design all aspects of electrical infrastructure including:Support production and supplier issue as an expert (4th line support).Transfer knowledge to production engineers.Develop Asia supplierâ€™s capability to deliver ASML modules with good quality and cost.Manage outsourcing of Electronics related modules.Design, document and maintain analog and/or digital board designs, electrical modules and infrastructure.Act as the Electronic Development representative, interacting intensively in a multidisciplinary design team.Specify and design interface electronics, including analog, digital and programmable logic based circuit design.Deliver the functional specification (EPS), test specification (TPS), design specification (EDS) and qualification document (TAR), Technical Product Documentation(TPD) and Design-BoM of the electrical infrastructure and electrical (sub) modules.Interact with WLT D&E colleagues from the Mechatronics, Software and Mechanical department.Ability to test & troubleshoot electrical & electronic systems to component level.Ability to support the integration & testing of electrical & electronic systems at the module, sub-system & system level.Ability to write test procedures, specifications and reports.Education and experienceMaster Degree in Electrical Engineeringâ€¢ At least 3-5 year experience in electrical system integration.â€¢ Basic knowledge of wiring diagrams and schematic diagrams.â€¢ Basic knowledge of ECAD design tools, with some experience using Mentor Graphics DX Designer, ORCad, PCad or similar ECAD s/w.â€¢ Basic knowledge of electrical drafting best practices.â€¢ Basic knowledge of industry codes and standards such as the National Electric Code, NFPA 79 Machine Tool Standards, IPC standards.Skillsâ€¢ Highly motivated electrical engineer with strong ownership and leadership mentality.â€¢ Candidate must have strong communicative skills in English with a commitment to achieving results on time.â€¢ Willingness to take on responsibility, follow through and keep multiple simultaneous assignments on schedule.â€¢ Desire to grow into position of task leadership & project planning.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Diversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://