D&E Field â€“ Taiwan Factory Engineering â€“ Mechatronics Engineer - Linkou,ASML Taiwan å�°ç�£è‰¾å�¸æ‘©çˆ¾,Semiconductor,Engineering,Other,Full-time,Entry level,"Linkou District, New Taipei, Taiwan",1,2 years of experience required,Negotiable,[],"Introduction to the jobFor our brand new ASML DUV manufacturing facility at New Taipei campus, we are looking for experienced mechatronics design engineers who can support the new manufacturing process of the DUV modules to meet the output and quality requirements for these DUV-modules.The vision is to build a more scalable, competitive and closer-to-the customer manufacturing capability in Taiwan which is able to send qualified modules directly to the customer.You will work in a team of approximately 40 fte (projected to grow further) of multiple competences. You will work closely together with the manufacturing team (~70 fte) and Supplier Quality Engineers (~10 fte). This team is part of the D&E Field organization with an overarching mission to increase intimacy with our customer and ASML operations (Customer Support, Repair & Re-use, Manufacturing and Strategic Sourcing and Procurement).This position is open to internal local hires as well as Long Term assignees (LTA) within ASML. If you are interested in an LTA-position, please refer to the LTA job description for Mechatronics Design Engineer in workday.Expect that you will spend approximately six months in the Netherlands or Wilton, USA for training purposes in 2026.Â Roles and responsibilitiesTo build the manufacturing capability at New Taipei Campus we need mechatronics engineers who will:Support the DUV module manufacturing organization with troubleshooting capability.Translate operational manufacturing requests into clear specifications in your own domain.Support and/or change of the current mechatronic design and ability to translate into mechanical electronic and software design changes.Identify design improvements that support more scalable and competitive systems. Translate these ideas into appropriate documentation and synchronize with central D&E.Can communicate and synchronize with engineers & architects from other disciplines (mechanics, electrical, software, physics, optics).Build and maintain specialist knowledge in the field of mechatronics (servo control, motion control, signal analysis) and manufacturing.Â Education and experienceYou have an inherent motivation for hands-on technical support, and you have bachelor's in mechatronics or a master's degree in either mechatronics engineering or mechanical engineering with a specialization in dynamics and control.andâ‰¥ 3 years of mechatronic engineering experience in a similar role within ASML or related high-tech industry.SkillsTo thrive in this job, you will need the following skills:Being a generalist in your field of expertise, willing to dive into unknown problems and ability to operate in a multi-disciplinary team;Is familiar with quality and safety regulations associated with working in a manufacturing environment and design;Is familiar with manufacturing way of working;Ability to diagnose and understand the functional and engineering principles of various parts and modules of the manufactured systems;Ability to bring technical problems to a solution and explain and present your solutions to appropriate stakeholders;Writing skills;Skilled in Matlab and Matlab Simulink:Analytical way of thinking and convert your analysis in creative, inventive, and thinking out-of-the box way to realize solutions in an ambiguous environment where not all design documentation is up-to-speed;A pioneering mindset, self-propelling, a pragmatic approach, and showing initiative;Enthusiastic and ambitious professional who can communicate clear and concise to peers and customers combined with stakeholder management skills to operate across sites and sectors.Quick learner, in for a challenge, continuously drive for improvements, and enjoy achieving results together with your team.Working level knowledge in EnglishDiversity and inclusionASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote per-sons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.Other informationThis position may require access to controlled technology, as defined in the Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require the Company to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. Â§ 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.Inclusion and diversityASML is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that inclusion and diversity is a driving force in the success of our company.Need to know more about applying for a job at ASML? Read our frequently asked questions.",,https://www.cake.me/companies/ASML-Taiwan/jobs/j00327458-d-e-field-taiwan-factory-engineering-mechatronics-engin-3a1776a3a7d2909e2fe36c51ec69a5?locale=en,1001 ~ 5000 people,æ–°ç«¹å¸‚